* testbench.spice -- `klt pex` testbench body for the sampling front end
* sub-block (issue #1017): the acquisition-window settling experiment of
* sim/sampling-acquisition-settling/run_acquisition_settling.py (issues
* #121/#236), re-cast around the layout's own extracted subckt interface so
* `klt pex` can swap the single `.include` below for its freshly
* `--parasitics`-extracted netlist and diff the schematic leg against the
* extracted leg, per corner.
*
* METHOD (same as the acquisition campaign, constants identical): SAMPLE
* pulse #1 (rise 10n, width 100n) acquires the OLD input value (VINP=0.2V,
* VINN=1.6V -- the worst-case rail-adjacent differential extremes the
* campaign uses); during the following HOLD the inputs step to the opposite
* extremes (130n, while Msw is off); SAMPLE pulse #2 re-asserts at 160n and
* the bootstrapped switches must pull TOP_P/TOP_N to the NEW value against
* the real Csamp load. The campaign's two measurement families, expressed
* as fixed `.meas` lines in the request run_pex.py builds (the crossing
* thresholds are constants because the stimulus amplitudes are constants
* held fixed across the PVT grid -- the campaign's own ratified-grid
* convention):
*   - t_settle_{p,n}_{50,90}: TRIG AT=160.1n (50% of SAMPLE#2's rising
*     edge) TARG V(top_x) VAL=<50%/90% of the old->new step> TD=160.1n
*     CROSS=1 -- the TD= qualifier is the campaign's own workaround for
*     ngspice counting CROSS=1 crossings from t=0 of the whole waveform;
*   - budget_{p,n}: v(top_x) at 160.1n + 83.3333n (one DR-006 worst-case
*     12 MHz phase period after the trigger) -- the residual the campaign
*     grades, a fixed-time read, not a crossing search;
*   - confirm_{p,n}: v(top_x) at 305n (well inside SAMPLE#2's width);
*   - boost_{p,n}_{budget,confirm}: the same fixed reads on BOOST_x, the
*     bootstrap rails the campaign instruments directly (issue #236's
*     precharge-leak finding) -- the extracted leg's BOOST rail carries
*     the bootstrap cap's real parasitic load, so the sch-vs-ext delta
*     there reads the booster's own routing parasitics.
*
* CORNER AXES: only `vdd` is keyed by corners.supply_v (a literal DC
* source, the alter gotcha -- layout/comparator/pex/README.md). Vcm and
* the VIN amplitudes stay at their fixed 0.9/0.2/1.6 V values at every
* corner, the campaign's own ratified-grid convention (its corners mode
* moves rail/process/temp only); a VCM or input amplitude that tracked the
* rail would change the stimulus definition the committed campaign record
* already measures with. SAMPLE's PWL amplitude stays 1.8 V for the same
* reason.
Vdd    vdd     0 DC 1.8
Vvcm   vcm     0 DC 0.9
Vinp   vinp    0 pwl(0 0.2 130n 0.2 130.2n 1.6 330n 1.6)
Vinn   vinn    0 pwl(0 1.6 130n 1.6 130.2n 0.2 330n 0.2)
Vsample sample 0 pwl(0 0 10n 0 10.2n 1.8 110n 1.8 110.2n 0 160n 0 160.2n 1.8 310n 1.8 310.2n 0 330n 0)

.include "sampling_frontend_pex_reference.spice"

* Pin order is the EXTRACTED netlist's own (alphabetical):
*   .SUBCKT gen_compose_0 BOOST_N BOOST_P BPREF_N BPREF_P GND SAMPLE
*   + TOP_N TOP_P VCM VDD VINN VINP
* run_pex.py asserts every run's extraction still declares exactly this
* list before anything simulates. BPREF_x are left on their own dead-end
* nets -- the *_NC wiring design/sar_adc_top.spice gives them, per
* sim/sampling-cdac-handoff's own documented interface contract.
Xdut boost_n boost_p bpref_n bpref_p 0 sample top_n top_p vcm vdd vinn vinp gen_compose_0
